"# Review log, round 2: places, events, periods\n\nIndependent fact-check of canon_places.csv (419), canon_events.csv (294), canon_periods.csv (220).\nBackups of the pre-review files: archive/prereview_round2/.\nScope: every R1 row; every R1/R2 row at low/medium confidence; every row claiming a UNESCO listing; the flagged rows; a random sample of 40 non-priority rows per file (seed 20260929; ids in work_r2pe/sel.json).\nUNESCO World Heritage claims checked against the full list by year (https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/?order=year, 1,276 properties); all confirmed except Nimrud (not inscribed). Intangible claims checked on ich.unesco.org.\n\nFormat: id | field | old | new | source URL\n\nPLC266 | defined_by | archaeologists (Layard; Mallowan); UNESCO | archaeologists (Layard; Mallowan) | https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/?order=year (Nimrud absent from the 1,276-property World Heritage List; tentative list only)\nPLC190 | defined_by | historians; UNESCO (to verify) | historians; UNESCO | https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1561\nPLC181 | notes | UNESCO inscription 2017 to verify. | UNESCO World Heritage 2017 (Valongo Wharf Archaeological Site), verified. | https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1548\n",
