"## Summary\n- Rows checked: 273 (priority 153: places 112, events 29, periods 12; random sample 120: 40 per file) plus PLC087 (linked to the Great Zimbabwe birds flag).\n- Rows changed: 39 (69 cells). Substantive errors (fact wrong, outdated or overstated): 25 rows; the other 14 changes resolve \"to verify\" notes with sources.\n- Error rate: random sample 3/120 (2.5%: PLC310, PRD037, PRD200); priority set 22/153 (c. 14%).\n- Flag outcomes not needing edits: Lomekwi 3 (hedged, fine); Kinngait Studios (fine); Pastoral and Camel periods (dates plausible, medium confidence kept).\n- Flag note: only two Saharan rock-art periods exist in canon_periods.csv (PRD020 Pastoral, PRD021 Camel). Round Head is STY081 in canon_movements_styles_schools.csv; Bubaline/Large Wild Fauna and Horse (Caballine) periods are not in the canon. Nothing was added.\n- Recent-event changes: the last Great Zimbabwe bird came back from Groote Schuur on 15 April 2026 (OCC169 now ends 2026; PLC087 updated).\n"
